fujinet-go-atari2600-desktop -- milestone log
=============================================

The plan is the family's (see fujinet-go-adam-desktop/PORTING.md): one C API
in core/, four native frontends, FujiNet in-process, one shared settings
store, a native debugger everywhere, no panels visible at startup,
clone-and-build CI. Nothing below is marked done on "it compiles".

M0  scaffold                                                          [x]
  [x] root CMakeLists (VERSION 0.1.0, FRONTEND switch, icon loop, CPack
      DEB/RPM/TGZ), .gitignore, LICENSE (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  [x] cmake/Dependencies.cmake: a2600_provide_dependency(); pins STELLA
      (tschak909/stella add-fujinet-support @ 65bd725e) and FUJINET
      (FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-firmware @ c68e8630, the commit the INTV port
      pins: master + TCP_NODELAY); STELLA_SRC / FUJINET_SRC dev overrides
  [x] cmake/StageStella.cmake: stages Stella's src/ into
      core/stella-generated keyed by pin + staging-file + shadow hashes
  [x] cmake/FujiNetRuntime.cmake + tools/fujinet/build-fujinet-desktop.sh
      (PC target RS232, BoIP 11504, web UI 11505) + the RS232 default-hosts
      patch, carried from the ColecoVision port
  [x] icons: tools/icons/make-icons.py renders the family mark INVERTED
      (outer discs and lines black, centre disc white) on #ffa645 to
      hicolor PNGs, .icns and app.ico
  [x] CI borrowed from the family: linux, windows, flatpak, macos, release.
      macos.yml and release.yml's macos-package run a two-leg matrix
      {arm64: macos-latest, x86_64: macos-15-intel} and confirm uname -m
      matches the leg; the release uploads one zip per architecture

M1  headless Stella core (the risk retirer)                          [x]
  [x] stella_core static library from the staged tree: emucore, common,
      debugger (+yacc), gui and debugger/gui (compiled because every
      Cart*.hxx pulls its widget under DEBUGGER_SUPPORT; they render
      offscreen and are never shown), FSNode for the platform, and our host
      classes. Defines SOUND_SUPPORT DEBUGGER_SUPPORT GUI_SUPPORT
      WINDOWED_SUPPORT VCS_CART_HOST_MAPPER FUJINET_SUPPORT + BSPF_*. No
      SDL, libpng, zlib, sqlite, httplib, cheats
  [x] core/stella/host: MediaFactory.hxx shadow selecting OSystemFNGO /
      FBBackendFNGO / FBSurfaceFNGO / SoundFNGO / EventHandlerFNGO
  [x] StellaHost: one thread owns Stella; jobs via withStella(); per-frame
      tia.update() until newFramePending; breakpoints -> Debugger::start()
      offscreen; frames published from the TIASurface; audio through
      Stella's own resamplers; console replacement disconnects the old
      CartridgeFUJI first (BoIP backlog is 1)
  [x] host_test: CONFIG boots, 60 frames in ~1 s, non-blank frame, break /
      step / frame / tia / break / run, reboot recreates the console and
      its debugger. debug_test: the C debugger contract end to end
  Gotchas met on the way (all fixed): CompositeKVRJsonAdapter wants an
  atomic repository (properties use the Noop one); kExitDebugger is a
  string_view; CpuDebug has no ps() getter (PS composed from the flags);
  the CONFIG cart has 7 selectable banks and the PC can be in bank 7; the
  help text is > 4 KB; completions come from BOTH DebuggerParser and
  Debugger

M2  session + FujiNet in-process                                     [x]
  [x] a2600session: settings, paths, media, fujinet_runtime (dlopen'd
      libfujinet, web UI bind from the family's entry wrapper), SDL audio,
      lifecycle. FujiNet first, wait for 11504, then the console
  [x] fujibus_smoke: libfujinet up, CartridgeFUJI reports the link up,
      and again after a reboot to CONFIG

M3  input                                                           [x]
  [x] bindings.c: flat target table (per port: joystick, paddles, driving,
      keypad; console switches; system actions), X11 keysyms, steal-on-
      rebind reporting EVERY victim (Space drives three left-port fires by
      default), packed "bindings" setting
  [x] hid_keys.c: evdev / Win scancode / macOS keycode -> keysym
  [x] gamepad_sdl.c: SDL3 thread, hotplug on SDL_EVENT_{JOYSTICK,GAMEPAD}_
      {ADDED,REMOVED}, raw-joystick fallback, capture for Map mode, type-
      dependent mapping (joystick / paddles analog / driving analog /
      keypad only through explicit bindings), generation counter
  [x] live controller types: Properties Controller_Left/Right +
      Console::setControllers + propSet().insert, reapplied after
      cartridgeSwapped; detected type exposed for the "Auto" label
  [x] session_test, bindings_test, gamepad_test, media_test green

M4  GNOME frontend (GTK4 / libadwaita)                              [x]
  [x] display on the frame clock (4:3 letterbox, 2:1 pixels), Machine /
      View / FujiNet menus, Preferences (TV format, per-port type with the
      detected type shown, analog switches, gamepad ports, volume, host),
      keypad window (both keypads, fire rows, console row, Map row),
      debugger window (Prompt with Tab completion, CPU & RAM, Disassembly
      with click-to-toggle breakpoints and bank selector, TIA with the
      picture, I/O, Breaks & Traps, States & Cart), FujiNet log and
      config, drag-and-drop, ESC reboots to CONFIG
  [x] run on the live desktop: "FujiNet connected" in the header, CONFIG
      client on screen

M5  KDE frontend (Qt6 Widgets)                                      [x]
  [x] same scope as GNOME. Keypad is a Qt::Dialog with a SetFixedSize
      layout so a tiling compositor floats it; the 3x4 blocks are tight and
      centred over the fire rows; the console row wraps to two rows of
      three when the font needs wider buttons, so nothing is elided
  [x] run on the live desktop beside the GNOME one

M6  Windows frontend (Win32 / GDI)                                  [x]
  [x] main.c (DwmFlush present thread, StretchDIBits, menus, settings and
      log windows, drag-and-drop, WM_ACTIVATE releases held keys),
      keypad_window.c (owner-drawn HELD buttons with mouse capture, fixed-
      size tool window, centred 3x4 blocks, Map mode with key and gamepad
      capture), dbg_window.c (tab control, edit subclassing for Enter and
      Tab completion, the same seven tabs)
  [x] cross-built with cmake/toolchains/mingw-w64.cmake + SDL's prebuilt
      SDL3-devel-3.4.12-mingw archive (WITH_FUJINET=OFF); runs under Wine
      with the keypad floating and the debugger open; core tests pass
      under Wine
  Two real Stella-for-Windows bugs found by the cross-build, fixed as
  shadow files in core/stella/host (see COMPLIANCE.md; both worth
  upstreaming):
  [x] FSNodeWINDOWS.hxx opens streams from a std::wstring -- an MSVC-only
      overload; libstdc++ (MSYS2 / mingw-w64) has only the C++17 path one
  [x] FujiNetLink::waitFor selected on the write set only; Winsock reports
      a refused non-blocking connect on the EXCEPTION set, so with no
      FujiNet listening every attempt waited out the 3 s timeout and the
      CONFIG client's screen stayed blank for seconds (host_test and
      session_test caught it under Wine)
  Also: the a2600debug_tia fields grp0/grp1 are graphics_p0/graphics_p1 --
  <dlgs.h> defines grp1 as a dialog resource id

M7  macOS frontend (AppKit)                                         [x]
  [x] main.m / AppDelegate.m / DisplayView.m (CVDisplayLink) / KeyForward.m
      (kVK_* through the HID table) / keypad (NSPanel, utility window,
      fixed size, floating level) / debugger (NSTabView, seven tabs),
      Info.plist.in, CMakeLists.txt bundling the .icns and packing the
      FujiNet runtime beside the executable
  [ ] compiled only by CI (macos.yml, both architectures) -- written on
      Linux, as every macOS frontend in the family was

M8  packaging, docs, release                                         [~]
  [x] README.md, COMPLIANCE.md, this log
  [x] flatpak manifests (GNOME with WebKitGTK, KDE opening the web UI in
      the browser), NSIS installer, CPack
  [ ] push, watch the five workflows, tag v0.1.0 -- the maintainer's call
